  "content": {
    "title": "McD's 'KPop Demon Hunters' menu arrives in Indiana. How much are the meals?",
    "text": "March 31, 2026, 8:46 a.m. ETThis week is gonna be golden for K-pop fans at McDonald’s.The chain began serving “KPop Demon Hunters”-inspired meals on March 31.Bringing South Korean flavors and the HUNTR/X-Saja Boys rivalry. A boba-style McFlurry, made with berry popping pearls and wild berry sauce, also hit the menu.Fans of the Netflix movie can show their support for HUNTR/X or Saja Boy with a purchase of one of two meals – the Saja Boys Breakfast Meal featuring a Spicy Sausage McMuffin with Egg, and the HUNTR/X Meal, with 10-piece McNuggets, the new limited-time Ramyeon McShaker Fries and two new sauces. The meals include exclusive photocards that unlock online content in the McDonald’s app.What’s in the McDonald’s “KPop Deamon Hunters” Meals? The Saja Boys Breakfast MealSpicy Saja McMuffin: A Sausage McMuffin with Egg, topped with a peppery Spicy Saja SauceHash BrownsSmall Soft DrinkThe HUNTR/X Meal10-piece Chicken McNuggetsMedium soft drinkRamyeon McShaker Fries: A spicy, umami spin on McDonald’s fries, featuring a soy, garlic, sesame and spice seasoning. Sprinkle the seasoning into the McShaker bag, add fries, and shake for a bold taste true to South Korean flavors.Hunter Sauce: A sweet chili sauce mixing notes of chili, garlic and pepper.Demon Sauce: A purple, bold mustard sauce with heat and tangEach meal comes with a collectible card pack consisting of an exclusive photocard for either HUNTR/X or the Saja Boys; and a Derpy access card with a QR code to unlock first access to exclusive content and a special reveal of the group that wins the sales battle.How much are the ‘Kpop’ Demon Hunters meals at McDonald’s?McDonald's \"Kpop Demon Hunters\" menu prices:The Saja Boys breakfast meal is about $7.59 in Indianapolis stores.The HUNTR/X meal is about $9.89.The Derpy McFlurry is about $5.39.Spicy Saja McMuffin. Those wanting to try the Spicy Saja McMuffin with Egg without the meal can order the sandwich for $3.99.Contact reporter Cheryl V. Jackson at cheryl.jackson@indystar.com or 317-444-6264. Follow her on X.com:@cherylvjackson or Bluesky:@cherylvjackson.bsky.social.",
